{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1350828-how-would-you-rp-interstellar-umbrood","id":1350828,"title":"How would you RP interstellar umbrood?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-25T08:35:43-08:00","id":1350828,"title":"How would you RP interstellar umbrood?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I'm currently working on a concept, of sorts, for my New Age based dreamspeaker/psychic and I would like as many ideas as possible on how to incorporate it into WOD lore.<br /> <br /> According to New Age/UFO religions, there's a being named &quot;Ashtar&quot; somewhere in the universe, who works with a group of enlightened spiritual beings called the Ascended Masters to protect humanity and fight it's spiritual foes. And so the theory goes, Ashtar has a space fleet connected with &quot;Ashtar Command,&quot; which is a group of channelers/mediums that relay messages from the upper echelons of Ashtar's fleet to all of humanity to inspire them. So, you're talking about a spiritual being with immense control over spiritual forces, which tend to manifest in the form of sci-fi aliens and starships.<br /> <br /> <br /> My question is, how would one incorporate Ashtar into the game? As a High Umbrood of sorts? If so, how do you explain the spaceships? Is it overkill for umbrood to manifest in spaceships, and use those spaceships in combat?<br /> <br /> And for character development, when do you think it would be appropriate for my character to make contact with such a &quot;fleet&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Here's a link for reference: <a href=\"https://www.znakovi-vremena.net/en/ashtar.htm\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.znakovi-vremena.net/en/ashtar.htm</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12664,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","user":"KingJohn","date":".  Link for reference. 11-25-2019, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:53:44-08:00","id":1350832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question is, how would one incorporate Ashtar into the game? </div> </div> </div>A Deep Umbra entity. That covers space pretty well (you could do that with the Astral too, but then you would have to accept the themes of Ashtar being a product of the mind/a dream/a fictional character...the Deep allows to explore more alien themes with impunity)<br /> <br /> Some powerful spirits (Lords and above) take notice of awakenings and send lesser spirits to teach them (indoctrinate, some would say). Ashtar it's one of those, he uses mediums and Ascended Masters to do this. Depending on how you rule Avatar's true nature, Ashtar's mediums may double as Avatars (there's an example in Gods and Monsters of a Godhead having it's shards form Avatars)<br /> <br /> Usually, you would interact with/summon these rather than Ashtar himself<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it overkill for umbrood to manifest in spaceships, and use those spaceships in combat? </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Especially not if he manifests in the Deep Umbra. You go big or go home in the Deep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And for character development, when do you think it would be appropriate for my character to make contact with such a &quot;fleet&quot;? </div> </div> </div>The way I would do it, by having Ashtar agents to contact the mages, and ally with them<br /> <br /> To go live there or summon the starfleet, nothing less than Spirit 5 would be required. But Ashtar should be able to provide help sooner, because we presume it's interested in humanity, and thus it's minions would be a lot closer to Earth<br /> <br /> Thus, from a chargen perspective, I would have: Ascended Masters as Mentors or Avatar, and less prominent members of the fleet or machines as Spiritual Allies. Ashtar himself could be a Totem<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 would be important to relate with Ashtar's fleet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-25-2019, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}